cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TempoDAG in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "TempoDAG: a compiler for streaming time-series models on FPGAs"
authors:
  - family-names: "Chamma"
    given-names: "Abdul-Rahman"
repository-code: "https://github.com/1509Chamma/TempoDAG"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-08-02"
keywords:
  - FPGA
  - high-level synthesis
  - compiler
  - time series
  - recurrent neural networks
  - state-space models
  - initiation interval
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  TempoDAG compiles streaming time-series models (recurrent cells,
  state-space models, temporal CNNs, attention variants) into verified
  fixed-point FPGA accelerators. Its temporal intermediate representation
  makes key hardware properties - initiation interval and resource usage -
  statically predictable, mechanically certifiable against machine-checked
  scheduling theorems, and empirically verifiable by C/RTL co-simulation,
  with predictions pre-registered before synthesis.
